FIGURE 1. Schematic model illustrating the curation of the sequence library and the design of ancestral ARODs, AncARODn0, AncARODn1, and AncARODn2 (A). First, homologous sequences of PtAROD were obtained through blastp analysis (proc. 1). After eliminating sequences that were either too long or too short, a sequence pair between PtAROD and one of the sequences in the library was prepared and sequence alignment was performed (proc. 2). If the sequence had “key residues,” the sequence was selected (proc. 3); and this process was applied to all the sequences in the library. ASR was performed with FastML utilizing the curated library. Consequently, three ancestral (red filled circles) and one native AROD (black filled circles, OkAROD) was generated.
FIGURE 2. pH dependency of ancestral (black) and native (red) ARODs (A). The activities of AncARODn0, AncARODn1, AncARODn2, and OkAROD are represented as filled squares, circles, upward-facing triangles, and downward-facing triangles, respectively. The relative activity was calculated by normalizing the highest activity as $100\%$ . Temperature-dependent activity changes for ancestral and native ARODs (B). The representation is identical to the case of Fig. 2A. To estimate $\mathrm{T}_{1/2}$ , the dotted line was drawn at the point where the relative activity would be $50\%$ .
FIGURE 3. Temperature-dependent enzyme kinetic plots of ancestral (AncARODn0 [A], AncARODn1 [B], AncARODn2 [C]) and native (OkAROD [D]) ARODs, respectively. The initial velocity at 10, 20, 30, and $40^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ was represented as filled squares, circles, upward-facing triangles, and downward-facing triangles, respectively. Arrhenius plots for $k_{\mathrm{{cat}}}$ of ancestral and native ARODs (E). Activation energies were calculated from the plots; the parameters are written in Table 2.
FIGURE 4, Schematic model representing biochemical parameters of ancestral and native ARODs on a phylogenetic tree. Thermal stability was gradually colored based on the difference in $\mathrm{T}_{1/2}$ ; the value is indicated in the star. Relative activity toward seven of the $20~\mathrm{L}$ -amino acids is represented as a bar graph.
